:"5a44e8afa517fd939a347ff57a1f5541f8d52d41","position":"1785858093136951001-4735bdaa-134c-46d3-941c-851f83e30d3b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"be823b086ccb1d83ac1478eda6ecda0a8cc8b304cf6862329d50a92de64caace","event_uuid":"eb5087e2-05dc-4ad9-a8f4-918642722674","position":{"commit_sha":"5a44e8afa517fd939a347ff57a1f5541f8d52d41","position":"1785858093790474001-eb5087e2-05dc-4ad9-a8f4-918642722674"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"3370c164056d95ca71b70990cd32c2ed8ba73c9f3ddb375b56d3d79e15bb3881","event_uuid":"2a87f0cf-b33a-4332-83dd-e140fa4a837d","position":{"commit_sha":"287d86340f096ab492135440881a4025150cd793","position":"1785858304294549001-2a87f0cf-b33a-4332-83dd-e140fa4a837d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"7819df6be460b271a8b3bdb9398c579bd65f759c825ab52c6fd2029952e9e7d5","event_uuid":"5a71ac86-439d-419b-9ab8-a979609acd03","position":{"commit_sha":"2c78a281e3435f4fa1656aaa73cab91b04d3c50d","position":"1785858650278922001-5a71ac86-439d-419b-9ab8-a979609acd03"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RCA (confirmed at runtime): the close landed-work precheck's commit scan (_referencing_commit_exists, src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py:149-175) calls the shared resolver resolve_ticket_id (src/rebar/_ids.py:191) for EVERY candidate ref extracted from EVERY reachable commit message. resolve_ticket_id prints ambiguity diagnostics directly to stderr (src/rebar/_ids.py:229-233 for 8-hex, :249-254 for alias, :270-274 'Ambiguous prefix ... matches multiple tickets'). Reproduced: a tracker with two tickets sharing a 4-hex prefix + a historical commit whose subject leads with that prefix -> scanning prints 'Error: Ambiguous prefix 2f3c matches multiple tickets: ...' while the scan still returns True for a full-ID trailer elsewhere in history. The return value is unaffected (ambiguous resolves return None either way), so this is pure diagnostic noise -- gate semantics are unchanged by the fix. Fix plan: add a keyword-only quiet=False parameter to resolve_ticket_id gating the three stderr prints; pass quiet=True ONLY from _referencing_commit_exists's scan loop. Explicit user-supplied ambiguous target ids (resolved elsewhere without quiet) keep full diagnostics.","timestamp":1785858304294549001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Fix implemented and pushed for review: Gerrit change 1363 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1363), commit 5a4758cdf4. Change: keyword-only quiet=False on resolve_ticket_id (src/rebar/_ids.py) gating the three stderr ambiguity diagnostics; _referencing_commit_exists passes quiet=True for its history-scan candidates only. RED->GREEN evidence: new tests/unit/test_transition_close.py failed pre-fix (2 failed: ambiguity noise on stderr in both the found and not-found directions), passes post-fix (3 passed); mutation check (reverting quiet=True) returns the tests to RED. Gate decisions unchanged both directions: scan returns True for the full-ID trailer, False for an unreferenced id, identical pre/post fix. Explicit ambiguous-prefix resolution (no quiet) still prints its diagnostic (AC3). Targeted suites green (85 passed: close-gate subtree/heldout, completion gate, verify-commit-ticket, path-injection guards); make lint + make typecheck clean. Sibling sweep: verify_commit.py:106, descendants.py:83, bugfix_size_gate.py:159, artifact_emit.py:134 all resolve refs the user/author directly supplied (single commit or CLI arg), not a history-wide scan -- no siblings; parity holds because CLI/MCP/library closes all route through the same transition_close core.","timestamp":1785858650278922001}],"created_at":1785557608007298001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"879b6903-74bf-4a1e-b48c-c11e6891792d","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"86a5-9221-0037-4e38"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nWhile closing ticket 86a5-9221-0037-4e38 on current origin/main, the landed-work precheck scanned all reachable commit messages and printed three unrelated resolver errors such as `Error: Ambiguous prefix 2f3c matches multiple tickets`. The target ticket used a full ID and closed successfully, so these diagnostics came from unrelated historical commit references. `_referencing_commit_exists` calls the shared resolver for every extracted reference; the resolver writes ambiguity errors to stderr even though the precheck only needs to know whether a reference matches the accepted target IDs.\n\n## Approach\nMake the close precheck resolve unrelated historical candidates silently while preserving normal resolver diagnostics for user-facing commands. Add a regression test with an ambiguous historical short prefix before a valid full-ID trailer and prove close scanning neither emits the unrelated error nor misses the valid commit.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The close landed-work precheck does not print ambiguity diagnostics for unrelated historical commit references.\n- [ ] A later valid full-ID commit reference is still detected when earlier history contains an ambiguous short prefix.\n- [ ] Target-ID ambiguity remains visible in commands where the user explicitly supplies an ambiguous prefix.\n- [ ] Focused tests and `make lint` pass.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py","reason":"silence resolver diagnostics for unrelated historical commit refs during close precheck"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_transition_close.py","reason":"regression coverage for ambiguous historical prefixes and later valid full-ID reference"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"4735bdaa-134c-46d3-941c-851f83e30d3b","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["close-gate","diagnostics"],"ticket_id":"af11-ac5f-4e86-4d1d","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Close precheck prints unrelated ambiguous-prefix resolver errors","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["fd3ab462-43e4-4f97-83b5-81c5f7805550","a2a54dff-ef93-4cbb-b59f-266eb7a5d021","879b6903-74bf-4a1e-b48c-c11e6891792d","8c937087-b3b3-4277-8db2-a79b1dbd5315","4735bdaa-134c-46d3-941c-851f83e30d3b","eb5087e2-05dc-4ad9-a8f4-918642722674","2a87f0cf-b33a-4332-83dd-e140fa4a837d","5a71ac86-439d-419b-9ab8-a979609acd03"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785858650278922002,"uuid":"385810bf-f89f-4d75-8dfb-b09af4b40e2d"}